Subject: [PATCH] d3d9: record coordinate wrap render states

Windows accepts WRAP0 through WRAP15 as render state and replays them when
applying a state block, including when the application never draws with
wrapping enabled. Preserve the values in the render state table. Keep the
warning about the separate, unimplemented interpolation behavior.

Evidence: docs/acceptance.md.

---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9State.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9State.cpp
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9State.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/D3D9State.cpp
@@ -234,14 +234,15 @@ D3D9SetRenderState(HANDLE hDevice, const D3DDDIARG_RENDERSTATE *data)
    case D3DDDIRS_WRAP13:
    case D3DDDIRS_WRAP14:
    case D3DDDIRS_WRAP15:
+      /* State blocks can record and restore wrap flags even when no
+       * primitive uses them. Retain them independently of interpolation. */
       if (data->Value) {
          static volatile LONG logged;
          D3D9WarnOncef(
             &logged,
             "unsupported D3D9 coordinate wrapping owner=d3d9-state "
             "reason=cylindrical-wrap-lowering-not-implemented "
-            "action=reject state=%u value=0x%08x\n",
+            "fallback=interpolate-without-wrapping state=%u value=0x%08x\n",
             data->State, data->Value);
-         return E_NOTIMPL;
       }
       break;
    case D3DDDIRS_PATCHEDGESTYLE:
